---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Link from "../../components/Link.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Ley Abierta — 190 years of Spanish law as Git | Alejandro Martínez"
  description="Solo engineer behind Ley Abierta: 12,260 Spanish laws reconstructed as 42,866 Git commits, searchable via a hybrid BM25 + RAG engine with a custom int8 SIMD C kernel. Recall@5 from 2% to 66% on real citizen queries; median latency from ~120s to sub-second. Live at leyabierta.es."
>
  <div class="page"> 

    <!-- top bar -->
    <header class="topbar">
      <Brand />
      <nav class="topbar-nav">
        <Link href="/">← back</Link>
        <Link href="/#case-studies">case studies</Link>
        <Link href="mailto:alex@konar.es">contact</Link>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- hero -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-tag">CASE STUDY · 04</div>
        <div class="hero-main">
          <div class="hero-meta">LEGISLATIVE TRANSPARENCY &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; SOLE ENGINEER</div>
          <h1 class="hero-h1">190 years of Spanish law as a Git repository.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Ley Abierta reconstructs every Spanish law since 1835 as a Markdown file with a
            Git commit dated to its official BOE publication — 12,260 laws, 42,866 commits,
            18 jurisdictions. On top of the repository lives a hybrid BM25 + RAG retrieval engine
            with a hand-rolled int8 SIMD C kernel: Recall@5 went from 2% to 66% on real citizen
            queries, and median latency dropped from ~120s to sub-second over three sprints.
            AGPL-3.0. Live at leyabierta.es.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <div class="hero-links-label">LINKS</div>
          <Link href="https://leyabierta.es" class="hero-link">leyabierta.es ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://github.com/leyabierta" class="hero-link">github.com/leyabierta ↗</Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- numbers strip -->
    <div class="numbers">
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">LAWS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">12,260</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">scraped from BOE since 1835</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">COMMITS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">42,866</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">dated to publication</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">YEARS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">190</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">of Spanish legislation</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">RECALL@5</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">2% → 66%</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">50 real citizen queries</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">LATENCY (P50)</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">~120s → &lt;1s</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">via custom int8 SIMD C kernel</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell numbers-cell--last">
        <div class="numbers-key">LICENSE</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">AGPL-3.0</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">permanently open</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the brief -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="THE BRIEF" title="Public law that's practically inaccessible.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Spanish legislation is nominally public: the BOE publishes every law as a PDF. But
        there's no API, no diff between versions, no way to ask "what changed in labor law
        in 2018?" and get a useful answer. The official site returns keyword matches in legal
        prose, not structured documents. Ley Abierta treats the law as source code — each
        reform is a commit, each jurisdiction a folder, each version a checkable diff. The
        result is 190 years of legislation that's queryable, diffable, and free.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- architecture -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="ARCHITECTURE" title="BOE to queryable repository in four stages.">
      <pre class="arch-diagram">  BOE open data API  (XML/JSON · no auth required)
          │
          ▼
  ┌─ pipeline  [ TypeScript · Bun ] ──────────────────────────────────┐
  │   fetch XML → parse → Markdown + YAML frontmatter                 │
  │   git commit --date=BOE_PUBLICATION_DATE                          │
  │   pre-1970 laws: date in frontmatter, git date = 1970-01-02       │
  │   ELI folder structure  (es/ · es-pv/ · es-ct/ · ×18 CCAA)       │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │                                │
          ▼                                ▼
  leyes/ git repo                   JSON cache (scratch)
  (public human-readable artifact)
          │
          ▼
  ┌─ api  [ Elysia · SQLite · FTS5 ] ────────────────────────────────┐
  │                                                                    │
  │   BM25 full-text search (FTS5)                                    │
  │         +                                                         │
  │   semantic search  — 483k int8 vectors                            │
  │   ┌────────────────────────────────────┐                          │
  │   │  C SIMD int8 cosine kernel          │                          │
  │   │  -75% index size (5.95 GB → 1.49 GB)│                         │
  │   │  SharedArrayBuffer worker pool      │                          │
  │   └────────────────────────────────────┘                          │
  │         +                                                         │
  │   RRF fusion  →  Recall@5: 2% → 66%  ·  P50 latency: ~120s → &lt;1s │
  │                                                                    │
  │   Embeddings: Gemini via OpenRouter                               │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │
          ▼
  ┌─ web  [ Astro SSG · Cloudflare Pages ] ──────────────────────────┐
  │   law content from leyes/ checkout at build time                  │
  │   derived data fetched from API at build time                     │
  │   live at leyabierta.es                                           │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Infrastructure: self-hosted Docker · Watchtower · GitHub Actions cron
                  (daily BOE ingestion) · Resend (email alerts)
</pre>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- decisions -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="DECISIONS" title="Six calls that define the project.">
      <div class="decisions-grid">
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">01 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Git as the storage layer</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Laws are versioned documents. Git is the right shape — not a relational DB, not a document store. <code>git log -- Codigo_Penal.md</code> is a meaningful civic tool. <code>git diff</code> between two commits is a legislative audit trail. The repo is the product, not just a backend artifact.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">02 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Custom SIMD C kernel</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Off-the-shelf vector libraries were too slow at 483k vectors on a single VM. A hand-rolled int8 cosine kernel with SIMD intrinsics cut the index from 5.95 GB to 1.49 GB (-75%) and made per-query latency acceptable without a GPU or a cloud vector DB. <code>SharedArrayBuffer</code> worker pool sharing eliminated re-initialization overhead between requests.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">03 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">BM25 + RAG hybrid retrieval</div>
          <p class="decision-body">BM25 alone on legal prose returned exact-term matches that missed citizen-language queries ("no me devuelven la fianza"). Semantic alone drifted on multi-article laws. RRF fusion of FTS5 BM25 + semantic retrieval took Recall@5 on 50 real citizen queries from 2% to 66% across three sprints, while median latency dropped from ~120s to sub-second after the int8 quantization pass.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">04 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Gemini embeddings via OpenRouter</div>
          <p class="decision-body">The 483k embedding vectors are generated via Gemini through OpenRouter — a pragmatic call for cost at this scale. The SIMD kernel handles retrieval on-prem; only the embedding generation hits an external API. Future direction is a fully self-hosted inference server (Qwen) to close that dependency.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">05 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">AGPL-3.0</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Public legal infrastructure shouldn't be capturable by a SaaS. AGPL guarantees that any deployment that serves Ley Abierta over a network must publish its modifications. The license matches the project's politics: if public law is a commons, so is the engine that makes it searchable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">06 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Bun + SQLite + FTS5 on one VM</div>
          <p class="decision-body">A single self-hosted VM with Elysia, SQLite, FTS5 and a Docker-managed SIMD process beats the obvious cloud-native option at this scale. No managed vector DB, no separate search service, no Kubernetes. Watchtower handles container updates; GitHub Actions handles daily ingestion. The stack is boring in the right ways.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ownership -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OWNERSHIP" title="One monorepo, four packages, sole author.">
      <div class="ownership">
        <div class="ownership-header">
          <span>PACKAGE</span>
          <span>STACK</span>
          <span class="text-right">COMMITS</span>
          <span class="text-right">ROLE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">pipeline</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">typescript · bun · git</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">api</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">elysia · sqlite · fts5 · c simd · openrouter</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">web</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">astro ssg · cloudflare pages</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">shared</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">typescript · bun</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">leyes/ (git repo)</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">markdown · yaml frontmatter · eli folder structure</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">42,866</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- outcome -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OUTCOME" title="190 years of law, queryable in real time.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Ley Abierta turns 190 years of Spanish legislation, technically public and practically
        unusable, into a queryable Git repository with a search layer that holds up on real
        citizen language. Recall@5 went from 2% to 66% on a 50-query benchmark of the kind
        of questions people actually ask. Median latency dropped from ~120s to sub-second on a
        single self-hosted VM without a managed vector DB or a GPU. The whole stack is AGPL-3.0
        and live at leyabierta.es: a working piece of public legal infrastructure, built solo.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- next case -->
    <div class="next-case">
      <span class="next-case-label">NEXT CASE STUDY</span>
      <Link href="/cases/asset-reality" class="next-case-link">
        05 &nbsp; Asset Reality — multi-sig engine for a custody platform that 2× AUM →
      </Link>
    </div>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="footer">
      <span>alejandro martinez · @lyricalstring · oss under konar technologies</span>
      <span>alex@konar.es</span>
    </footer>

  </div>

</Base>


<style>
  /* - REVEAL SECTIONS - */
  .reveal-section {
    margin-block: 48px;
  }

  .page {
    max-width: 1280px;
    padding: 28px 32px 56px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* ── TOP BAR ── */
  .topbar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .topbar-left {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .topbar-nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  /* ── HERO ── */
  .hero {
    padding-top: 88px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr 280px;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .hero-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .hero-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .hero-h1 {
    font-size: 64px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    max-width: 880px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .hero-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-top: 24px;
    max-width: 680px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .hero-links {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .hero-links-label {
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .hero-link {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* ── NUMBERS STRIP ── */
  .numbers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .numbers-cell {
    padding: 24px 16px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .numbers-cell--last {
    border-right: none;
  }

  .numbers-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .numbers-val {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .numbers-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  /* ── BODY PARA (brief + outcome) ── */
  .body-para {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 640px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .outcome-caveat {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  /* ── ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM ── */
  .arch-diagram {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.85;
    background: #101216;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    max-width: 760px;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── DECISIONS ── */
  .decisions-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px 56px;
    max-width: 920px;
  }

  .decision-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .decision-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .decision-body {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 8px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .decision-body code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--fg);
    background: #101216;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  /* ── OWNERSHIP TABLE ── */
  .ownership {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--dim);
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .ownership-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 2fr 1fr 1fr;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .ownership-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 2fr 1fr 1fr;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .ownership-repo {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .ownership-dim {
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .text-right {
    text-align: right;
  }

  /* ── NEXT CASE ── */
  .next-case {
    margin-top: 88px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .next-case-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .next-case-link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* ── FOOTER ── */
  .footer {
    margin-top: 88px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }
</style>
